Licensing choice

XA Display Host (macos/) is original code written for this repository and is
MIT, same as the rest of this tree. It is not a fork of OpenDisplay
(GPL-3.0). No OpenDisplay, Deskreen, libusbmuxd, or other GPL/LGPL source is
vendored here.

The video wire format (4-byte big-endian length, JSON control messages, and
H.264 Annex-B access units on TCP port 9000, Bonjour type _opensidecar._tcp)
is implemented from the behavior documented by the MIT client so an existing
OpenDisplay 1.30.x sender can still drive basic video, touch, and scroll.
That does not copy OpenDisplay's source.

The Mac host talks to Apple's built-in usbmuxd. It does not ship the
libimobiledevice usbmuxd daemon or libusbmuxd.

CGVirtualDisplay is Apple private API, isolated in XAVirtualDisplay.m.
Declarations there are this project's own and are not taken from a GPL tree.
